  "version": "0.7.2-beta.11",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.2-beta.10`\n\n### Fixes\n\n- batch output nobody typed for even after a quiet spell: the output sender sent the first bytes after a pause at once so an echo never waited, but that also split frames a program writes in pieces, such as a spinner's return, erase and draw or a TUI's animation and the move back to its input box, and the cursor showed where the frame was still being drawn; only output within 150 ms of input to the session, typed or broadcast, now skips the 8 ms window ([d7fac460](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/d7fac4601369f3c0623367624abc267b0b8d79a6))\n- stop the cursor flashing at column 0 while a line redraws: a program redrawing a line, as npm's spinner does, first returns to column 0 and then draws, and when the return reached xterm as a chunk of its own the cursor was rendered there for a frame, covering the spinner a dozen times a second; a chunk that draws nothing and only returns to a line's start, erases or toggles the cursor is now held until the drawing that follows it, for at most 50 ms and never right after a keystroke, while a move that ends in another column, such as a TUI putting the cursor back in its input box, still goes out at once ([add30bc3](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/add30bc3fc3bf7811d84e67453c44c0503a83e44))\n\n### UI and usability\n\n- replace the app icon with a hand-drawn hermit crab whose shell is a terminal window: the yellow key read as a password manager rather than a terminal and its >_ blurred at small sizes; the new sticker-style crab on a beach makes the shell pun (a crab's home and the command line, with a new shell like a new host over SSH), the 16 to 32 px icons use a simplified crab with only the shell, eyes and one claw so they stay legible, and app-icon.svg is the source for every size ([1311bf07](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/1311bf070f4858eae3cbcc437c6d15462dfde13a))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.2-beta.10...v0.7.2-beta.11](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.2-beta.10...v0.7.2-beta.11)",
